 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Houses are built on integer points of a line, initially empty, in the order of queries. A query at point p builds a house only when p is still empty and at least one of p - 1 and p + 1 is empty; otherwise the query builds nothing. After every query (built or not) record the length of the longest run of consecutive occupied points (0 while no house exists). Return the recorded lengths.",
  "provenance": [
